  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "During refinement in Star Form blessed land, the land spirit adds large numbers of variant humans to Fang Yuan’s poisonous blood: hairy men, rockmen, snowmen, inkmen, eggmen, feathermen, and mermen.",
      "chapters": [
        861
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "star-form-captives",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_star_form_blessed_land",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Shark Demon names a mermen sea area among Eastern Sea’s ten great sea areas. Countless mermen live there, and he ranks that population as one of Eastern Sea’s top ten super forces. He also says female mermen there are extremely amorous.",
      "chapters": [
        892
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "regional-standing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_shark_demon",
        "reg_eastern_sea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mermen are a type of variant human. Most mermen in the world live in Eastern Sea. They can live underwater and breathe. They coined the name demon stone for marrow sucking stone after suffering from it, and some merman tribes in Eastern Sea history worshipped those stones as deities.",
      "chapters": [
        1297
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "underwater-life",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "There were ten variant human races in the Gu world: hairy men, rockmen, snowmen, feathermen, mermen, inkmen, eggmen, beastmen, miniman, and mushroommen.",
      "chapters": [
        1489
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "variant-human-standing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ice Crystal Immortal Monarch tells the merman leaders that the merman race received Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable’s help, and that in the entire five regions only they are still a super force among the variant humans.",
      "chapters": [
        1979
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "variant-human-standing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ice_crystal_immortal_monarch",
        "char_paradise_earth_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "They have human bodies and fish tails. Scale colors vary: blue and red are common, white and black are very rare. Male and female are both called very beautiful and good looking.",
      "chapters": [
        1656
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "form",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Merfolk liked scales, luster, and contours forming a streamlined body shape. The merfolk aesthetic sense had nothing to do with hair.",
      "chapters": [
        2256
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "form",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A merman is a variant human that can breathe underwater naturally and live. Mermen are attached to rivers and water bodies and are most skilled at water path. White scaled mermen and mermaids can become saints and saintesses. Black scaled newborns are treated as cursed and are killed at birth, often by their parents.",
      "chapters": [
        1656
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "water-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the outside world, merfolk have lower status than humans, and the two sides often fight.",
      "chapters": [
        1656
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "water-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In merman society, females have higher status than males, and they elect a saintess but not a saint. Mermen are born with water path dao marks.",
      "chapters": [
        2241
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "water-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_dao_marks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Among the mermen, an origin story places the first batch in Eastern Sea, where they built a small fishing village. A sea beast attack, a mermaid’s songs to a Sea God, and her sister finishing the third song are the origin told for the Sea God Ceremony and its saintess singing contest.",
      "chapters": [
        1665
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "origin-legend",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
